# First x86_64 EXECUTION pass on the 2026-08-07/08 aarch64 campaign
# ================================================================
# Scope: verify docs/X64_APPLICABILITY.md. Sections A/B of that file were
# predictions; this is the first pass that RAN x86_64 code. Verdicts and the
# full narrative live in that file's section F -- this is the raw record.
#
# LANDED 2026-08-12, AFTER THE DEFECT IT FOUND WAS FIXED. The four t=8 ERROR
# rows below are NOT an open defect any more: PR #497 (merged b700489) root-
# caused them to the x86 loop-filter V window sizing its rectangle from a
# plane-worst-case constant instead of the mask, named both writers, and
# narrowed the window. See docs/X64_APPLICABILITY.md section G. The rows are
# kept verbatim as the discovery record.
#
# base commit    : 5e9975f  (brief named 312dcc3; main moved mid-session, all
#                            worktrees share one .git -- every number here is
#                            against 5e9975f)
# branch         : verify/x64-applicability
# date           : 2026-08-10
#
# HOST / EXECUTION ENVIRONMENT
#   host         : Apple M4 Pro (8P+4E), macOS 26.5.2, aarch64
#   Rosetta 2    : ABSENT (`arch -x86_64 /usr/bin/true` -> "Bad CPU type in
#                  executable"; no /Library/Apple/usr/libexec/oah). So
#                  x86_64-apple-darwin binaries build and CANNOT run.
#   x86_64 exec  : colima QEMU-TCG Linux VM, profile `x86`, 4 vCPU, 6 GiB.
#                  Guest CPU: "QEMU TCG CPU version 2.5+", AuthenticAMD,
#                  clflush size 64. Feature set: sse..sse4_2, avx, avx2, fma,
#                  bmi1, bmi2, aes, f16c, movbe, abm.  NO AVX-512.
#   build path   : cross-compiled on the HOST to x86_64-unknown-linux-musl with
#                  `zig cc -target x86_64-linux-musl` (zig 0.16.0) as CC/AR and
#                  linker, plus -C link-self-contained=no (Rust's musl rcrt1.o
#                  and zig's crt1.o both define _start). ~34 s per binary.
#                  Recipe committed: scripts/x64/build_and_run_x86.sh
#
# WHAT THESE NUMBERS ARE AND ARE NOT
#   VALID  : bit-exactness (md5 vs the dav1d reference), PASS/FAIL by name,
#            borrow-tracker + threading behaviour, deterministic counters,
#            symbol/static facts.
#   INVALID: every wall_ms column below, for any perf purpose. TCG is a JIT
#            interpreter with no cache model, no store buffer, no branch
#            predictor and no PMU. The wall_ms values are kept only as a
#            relative progress signal and are ~25x inflated vs native.
#            NOTHING about the gap to dav1d, and nothing about A1's shift
#            ladder, can be concluded from this record.
#   PARTIAL: AVX-512 is UNEXECUTED. 1,754 _mm512_* call sites (mc 671,
#            looprestoration 391, itx 390, ipred 206, cdef 51, loopfilter 45)
#            were never entered; every correctness verdict here is about the
#            AVX2 tier only.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. CORPUS  (examples/md5_inventory, all 19 meson groups, film grain applied
#             on the two film_grain/ groups exactly as decode_md5_verify does)
#    file: x64_verify_2026-08-10_corpus.tsv.zst
#    cols: arm arch threads group name status expected actual frames wall_ms
#
#    arch     threads  PASS  MISMATCH  ERROR  SKIP   arm
#    x86_64   1        766   0         0      2      default  (2 containers: --group 8-bit/data 358 + --skip-group 8-bit/data 408+2 SKIP)
#    x86_64   8        762   0         4      2      default
#    x86_64   8        204*  0         3      0      norecon (partial, RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=0, stopped at 207 rows)
#    aarch64  1        766   0         0      2      default
#    aarch64  8        753   0         0      2      default_skipfg  (x2 runs)
#    aarch64  16       753   0         0      2      default_skipfg
#    aarch64  32       753   0         0      2      default_skipfg
#
#    The 2 SKIPs are 8-bit/features/{annexb,section5} (not .ivf) on both arches.
#    aarch64 t>1 needs --skip-group film_grain because of #479 (see 3 below).
#
#    MISMATCH is ZERO on x86_64 at both thread counts => section B of
#    X64_APPLICABILITY.md is CONFIRMED for the AVX2 tier: all eight listed
#    defects were aarch64-only.
#
# 2. x86-ONLY DEFECT: 4 vectors abort at t=8 (set-diffed BY NAME vs aarch64 t=8)
#      8-bit/data/00000325                                                ERROR vs PASS
#      8-bit/data/00000625                                                ERROR vs PASS
#      8-bit/issues/issue_48                                              ERROR vs PASS
#      8-bit/vq_suite/Syntax_AV1_mainb8ss420_432x240_019_vq_aom_ctest_4.2  ERROR vs PASS
#    plus, in the RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=0 arm: 00000557, 00000580, 00000624.
#    Seven distinct vectors; the failing SET is not stable => timing window,
#    not content. All four of the first set PASS in isolation (12 retries).
#
#    Each is a worker `overlapping DisjointMut` panic surfaced as
#    "decode error: generic error". Extents (default arm):
#        &    _[82432..82560] (128 B) vs &mut _[82488..82496]   (8 B)
#        &mut _[73844..73848]   (4 B) vs &    _[73728..73848] (120 B)
#        &    _[16640..16752] (112 B) vs &mut _[16672..16688]  (16 B)
#        &    _[49536..49660] (124 B) vs &mut _[49536..49568]  (32 B)
#    and (norecon arm, with RUST_BACKTRACE=1):
#        &    _[73728..73736]   (8 B) vs &mut _[73728..73736]   (8 B)  <-- IDENTICAL
#        &    _[73728..73744]  (16 B) vs &mut _[73728..73732]   (4 B)
#
#    SITE (from the backtrace, file x64_verify_2026-08-10_panics.txt):
#        rav1d_worker_task              src/thread_task.rs:1370
#        rav1d_filter_sbrow_deblock_rows src/recon.rs:3753
#        rav1d_loopfilter_sbrow_rows    src/lf_apply.rs:711
#        filter_plane_rows_y            src/lf_apply.rs:439
#        loopfilter_sb_direct           src/loopfilter.rs:103
#        loopfilter_sb_dispatch         src/safe_simd/loopfilter.rs:5134  (x86-only file)
#        compact_read_per_row           include/dav1d/picture.rs:1176
#    The identical-extent pair cannot be over-reservation: it is a genuine
#    read/write race on picture pixels, which an `unchecked` build would not
#    panic on. #482 is ruled OUT (RAV1D_OWNED_RECON=0 fails at a higher rate).
#    NOT yet established: who the writer is (needs --features probe-sites,
#    which keeps per-record Locs) and whether removing the check_tile deblock
#    barrier (A2) is the enabling change (needs the barrier put back).
#
# 3. #479 (film-grain multi-thread) is aarch64-ONLY -- measured both ways
#    file: x64_verify_2026-08-10_corpus.tsv.zst, arm=filmgrain
#      x86_64  t=1 13/13 PASS   t=4 13/13 PASS   t=8 13/13 PASS
#      aarch64 t=1 13/13 PASS   t=4 exit 101     t=8 exit 101
#    aarch64 dies with `overlapping DisjointMut` at picture.rs:742 before
#    finishing one vector. Source: src/safe_simd/filmgrain.rs (x86) already
#    guards a BAND -- total_pixels = (bh-1)*pixel_stride + pw from
#    row_num*FG_BLOCK_SIZE*stride, for dst/src/fguv-luma alike -- while
#    src/safe_simd/filmgrain_arm.rs takes full_guard_mut/full_guard, i.e. the
#    whole picture component, per band. The x86 kernel has always had the shape
#    PR #491 introduces on aarch64. The campaign's `--skip-group film_grain`
#    habit was an aarch64-only tax.
#
# 4. TIER CENSUS (proves which SIMD tier executed; --features __probe_x86tier)
#    file: x64_verify_2026-08-10_tiercensus.tsv
#    8-bit/data/00000001, 3 frames, t=1, x86_64:
#      Scalar / X86V2 : 0 avx2 grants,    337,378 refusals
#      X86V3/V4/Native: 384,221 grants,   0 refusals; avx512 0/173,257;
#                       avx512x 0/123,675
#      md5 identical at all five levels.
#    => A6 REFUTED on x86 (the mask IS in the x86 dispatch path, so
#       CpuLevel::Scalar really is scalar there), and X86V2 == Scalar because
#       nothing in safe_simd dispatches below the AVX2 token.
#
# 5. A4 GATE, PROVEN TO HAVE TEETH ON x86
#      crates/rav1d-disjoint-mut/tests/wide_exclusion.rs on x86_64: ok, 0.61 s
#      mutation (in-lock `state` re-read at tracker_shard.rs:1476 -> `if false`)
#      rebuilt: FAILED 3/3 runs. Mutation reverted; green again.
#
# 6. c-ffi ON x86 LINUX
#      CI's exact leg, `cargo clippy --no-default-features
#      --features "c-ffi,bitdepth_8,bitdepth_16" -- -D warnings`:
#        --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl : exit 0
#        macOS aarch64 host                 : exit 101,
#          error[E0080] assertion failed: Rav1dError::EAGAIN as u8 == libc::EAGAIN as u8
#      => that blocker is host-OS (Darwin EAGAIN 35 vs Linux 11), not arch.
#      Adding --all-targets (CI does not) surfaces 5 latent lints on x86:
#      token_test_lock unused (lib test cfg) + 4 in examples/{itx_shape_census,
#      md5_ablate}.rs.
#
# 7. #482 SEAM SYMBOLS (item 4, static half)
#      `nm | grep owned_recon` returns the SAME 8 symbols on the x86_64 and the
#      aarch64 release example binary, and no out-of-line ReconSrc::slice on
#      either => the #483 symptom (the seam accessor going out-of-line) does not
#      appear on x86. The 0.3-1.3% seam COST is a wall-clock number and is NOT
#      measured here. Liveness of the owned path on x86 is also unproven.
#
# 8. ONE UNEXPLAINED x86 STALL (recorded, not attributed)
#      A t=1 pass stopped progressing on 8-bit/data/00001114 (34 ms on aarch64)
#      with 0.00% CPU, exactly ONE thread, wchan __do_sys_pause -- and the static
#      binary has no call site to pause() at all (llvm-objdump: zero
#      callq/jmp <pause>), so the wait channel is not explicable from our code.
#      The vector passes in isolation and the re-run passed the same group.
#      Most likely colima/virtiofs/TCG; kept here because it is the one
#      observation in this pass I could not pin down.
#
# METHOD NOTES
#   * Set-diffs are BY NAME (group/name key), never by count.
#   * No `nice` on anything whose timing mattered -- nothing here is timed.
#   * measlock was NOT taken: this pass produces no timing numbers, so it needs
#     no exclusive box. Two host-side cargo builds ran niced during the runs.
#   * TRAP RECORDED: a `cargo build` mid-session replaced
#     examples/md5_inventory under three live container runs. They survived (the
#     old inode stays mapped) but the arm identity was destroyed. Distinct
#     _plain / _sites binary copies are the fix -- same class as "never edit a
#     shell script while it is running".
#
# 9. PREMISE CORRECTION (added after the runs, before commit)
#    The task that commissioned this pass asserted "essentially nothing has been
#    measured on x86_64; x86 has only ever been compile-checked". THAT IS FALSE,
#    and docs/X64_APPLICABILITY.md sections A-E cite none of the files that
#    prove it. CITED, NOT MEASURED HERE:
#      benchmarks/x64_i265_gap_2026-08-08.meta
#      benchmarks/x64_i265_postmerge_2026-08-08.meta
#      benchmarks/x64_i265_CORRECTION_2026-08-08.md
#      issue #458
#    Host i265 = Intel Core Ultra 7 265K, Ubuntu 26.04, idle, dedicated, dav1d
#    1.5.3 built on-box, ab_sweep.sh 3 rounds x 3 reps interleaved. Restricted
#    to the arms its own CORRECTION leaves standing (`main` a6a7e232, `pre445`;
#    `audit445`/`attrib` are VOID -- a silent git checkout refusal rebuilt
#    pre-merge main for both):
#      * x86 SINGLE-THREAD is NARROWER than aarch64 vs dav1d: 1.51x (8bpc),
#        1.99x (10bpc) vs the same-week aarch64 1.62x / 2.01x.
#      * x86 tile threading ANTI-SCALES: v4k_8tile 8bpc 220.1 / 428.7 / 590.6 /
#        622.2 ms/f at t=1/2/4/8 -> t1->t8 = 0.35x, i.e. t=8 is 2.8x SLOWER than
#        t=1, while dav1d scales 4.46x on the same box. The gap therefore goes
#        1.5x at t=1 to 19.0-20.8x at t=8 (aarch64: 3.44x).
#      * The campaign's sharded-tracker chain costs x86 +59% at t=1 (220.6 ->
#        350.8; 10bpc 275 -> 412), aarch64 flat over the same merge. The base
#        verified here (5e9975f) is post-merge, so that regression is in it.
#      * Frame md5 identical across arms x vectors x t{1,2,4,8} on x64, and
#        #446's CDEF pri_tap divergence does not exist there -- consistent with
#        section 1 above.
#    => The materially-different x86 shape the task asked for already exists on
#       record. A1's "applies", A2's "fully applicable" and A5's batch-factor
#       row must not be read as-is: on x86 the tracker chain is a measured net
#       LOSS at t=1, and the only x86 data on the barrier and the batching came
#       from the VOID arms, so nobody has a valid x86 measurement of either.
#
# 10. FOLLOW-UP ATTEMPT, NEGATIVE (recorded so it is not repeated blind)
#     `--features probe-sites` (which keeps per-record Locs and would name BOTH
#     sides of the F2 collision), one full pass `--group 8-bit/data --threads 8`
#     on x86_64: 358/358 PASS, 0 overlapping-DisjointMut. Did NOT reproduce.
#     Either the per-record Loc store perturbs the window, or ~2 hits per 358
#     vectors needs several passes. Also a third independent x86 t=8 run with
#     0 MISMATCH.
#     A targeted 12-pass loop over the four originally-failing vectors (t=8,
#     RUST_BACKTRACE=1, probe-sites) likewise produced 0 overlaps -- the window
#     needs the long sequential run, not the vector.
